{{- /*
  The page the platform's own hosts get while the platform is down: the apex
  and api, identity, mcp, os and vscode under it. errorpages.go says why.

  Everything is inline because nothing else may be reachable while this page
  is up: one stylesheet, the mark in the markup, no font file, no script, no
  image. The Content-Security-Policy the server sends allows this one
  stylesheet by hash and nothing else.
*/ -}}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
<meta name="theme-color" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)" content="#f7f7f5">
<meta name="theme-color" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" content="#07090a">
<title>{{.Title}}</title>
<meta name="description" content="{{.Message}}">
<style>
/*
  THE PALETTE IS THE BRAND'S, WRITTEN OUT. brand/tokens.css is the one source,
  but a page that may fetch nothing cannot import it, so these six values are
  copied from it and errorpages_test.go fails the build when they drift. They
  are written as a plain light set plus a dark override rather than as the
  tokens' light-dark(): a browser that does not know light-dark() would drop
  every colour, and this is the page that has to render for everybody.
*/
:root {
  --bg: #f7f7f5;
  --surface: #ffffff;
  --fg: #191d1a;
  --muted: #5b615c;
  --line: #e5e6e2;
  --accent: #047d5a;
  color-scheme: light dark;
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root {
    --bg: #07090a;
    --surface: #0b1110;
    --fg: #e8e6dd;
    --muted: #9ca395;
    --line: #18231e;
    --accent: #5ccda7;
  }
}

*, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
html { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; }

/*
  The brand's type stack, faces first. Nothing here can be fetched, so a
  machine without Inter or Squada One wears the system face; the wordmark
  is the only place that matters.
*/
body {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 1.5rem;
  min-height: 100vh;
  min-height: 100dvh;
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  background: var(--bg);
  color: var(--fg);
  font-family: "InterVariable", "Inter", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 0.9375rem;
  line-height: 1.5;
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
}

/* A border, not a shadow, and the brand's radius: the same card the sign-in page is. */
main {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 26rem;
  padding: 2.75rem 2rem 2.5rem;
  text-align: center;
  background: var(--surface);
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: 0.625rem;
}

.brand {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: 0.75rem;
  margin-bottom: 2rem;
}
.mark {
  display: block;
  width: 2.5rem;
  height: 2.5rem;
  color: var(--accent);
}
.mark svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
.name {
  font-family: "Squada One", "InterVariable", "Inter", ui-sans-serif, sans-serif;
  font-size: 2rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  line-height: 1;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
}

h1 {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: 1.25rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  line-height: 1.35;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  text-wrap: balance;
}
p {
  margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
  color: var(--muted);
  text-wrap: pretty;
}

/* A slow breath on the mark: a thing that is running, saying so. Held still for anyone who asks. */
@keyframes breathe { 50% { opacity: 0.55; } }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
  .mark { animation: breathe 4s ease-in-out infinite; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<div class="brand">
<span class="mark">{{.Mark}}</span>
<span class="name">MemQL</span>
</div>
<h1>{{.Heading}}</h1>
<p>{{.Detail}}</p>
</main>
</body>
</html>
